Create a new note titled "{{title}}".

Steps:
1. Call list_md_files to check whether a note with a similar name already exists.
   If one does, ask the user whether to update it instead.
2. Derive a kebab-case file_id from the title (e.g. "Spring Boot" → "spring-boot.md").
3. Call create_md_file with:
   - file_id    : the derived kebab-case filename
   - title      : "{{title}}"
{{#hasBody}}
   - body       : {{body}}
{{/hasBody}}
{{#hasTags}}
   - tags       : split "{{tags}}" into a list (no # prefix)
{{/hasTags}}
{{#hasLinks}}
   - wiki_links : split "{{links}}" into a list of file IDs
{{/hasLinks}}
{{#hasMetadataFields}}
   - metadata   : a JSON object containing the following configured frontmatter fields:
{{#metadataFields}}
     * {{name}} — {{description}}{{#required}} (required){{/required}}
{{/metadataFields}}
     Auto-set "created" (or "date") to today's date if it appears in the list above.
     Leave optional fields blank unless the user supplied a value.
{{/hasMetadataFields}}
4. Report the created file ID and any auto-discovered wiki-links the server added.
